WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:21.261
Jonathan searched for Marissa as soon as he arrived at the soccer field Saturday afternoon. He spotted her on the sideline.

2
00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:25.854
"I'm going to walk Pastrami down the sideline to get his energy out," he said to his parents.

3
00:00:25.855 --> 00:00:31.242
"Energy?" Mr. Cho echoed. "In this heat even the dog has no energy."

4
00:00:31.243 --> 00:00:35.409
Pastrami lay on the grass, looking as energetic as an old tortoise.

5
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.583
"I think he really wants to go for a walk," Jonathan said quickly.

6
00:00:39.584 --> 00:00:43.994
"Aren't you supposed to start warming up with your team?" asked his mom.

7
00:00:43.995 --> 00:00:52.144
Jonathan ignored her, yanking on Pastrami's leash as they trudged down the sideline.

8
00:00:52.145 --> 00:01:00.303
They passed Carlos and his family. His mother fanned herself and called to Jonathan, "Oh, this horrible weather!

9
00:01:00.304 --> 00:01:03.555
How will you and my baby Carlos run in this heat?"

10
00:01:03.556 --> 00:01:14.375
"We'll be fine, Mrs. Ruiz!" Jonathan laughed. Mrs. Cho called Jonathan Johnnyboy, but at least she never called him a baby!

11
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:20.459
Jonathan walked over to Marissa, who looked especially cute today in a bright red sundress and a high ponytail.

12
00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.213
He had to get this apology over with.

13
00:01:23.214 --> 00:01:26.379
Jonathan waved at her awkwardly, but she turned away.

14
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:33.299
Pastrami yapped and wagged his tail. Still Marissa kept her back to them.

15
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:41.601
Jonathan quickly started walking Pastrami farther down the sideline, pretending that he'd just been walking the dog.

16
00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:44.625
Marissa obviously wanted nothing to do with Jonathan.

17
00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:49.447
Though she probably would have loved seeing Pastrami again if Jonathan weren't holding his leash.

18
00:01:49.447 --> 00:01:56.864
Back at his parents' chairs, Jonathan gave Pastrami a drink and then splashed some water on his own face.

19
00:01:56.865 --> 00:02:01.758
He was really hot—and his embarrassment over Marissa wasn't helping one bit.

20
00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:10.588
After warm-up drills Jonathan felt even hotter. Sweat dripped from his forehead as he walked to the center of the field.

21
00:02:10.589 --> 00:02:17.660
Today his team was playing the Silver Bombers, another name that sounded a million times cooler than Team Wattenbarger.

22
00:02:17.661 --> 00:02:25.073
The Silver Bombers had three substitutes—three more than Jonathan's team had, now that Andrew and Aaron had quit the team.

23
00:02:25.074 --> 00:02:34.136
The game began. Jonathan panted as he chased the ball up and down the hot field.

24
00:02:34.137 --> 00:02:37.343
He wished Andrew and Aaron had stayed on the team.

25
00:02:37.344 --> 00:02:44.301
He wished he had a different coach. He wished Max would share the ball. He wished Marissa would wave back at him.

26
00:02:44.302 --> 00:02:48.220
He wished it were cooler outside. He wished—

27
00:02:48.221 --> 00:02:53.559
"Jonathan, pay attention!" Coach Wattenbarger barked as the ball sailed toward him.

28
00:02:53.560 --> 00:03:02.888
Jonathan trapped the ball and glanced at the goal. He wasn't very close, but he might be able to shoot the ball in.

29
00:03:02.889 --> 00:03:06.069
"Pass it to Max!" the coach screamed.

30
00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:12.708
Max was double-teamed by the Silver Bombers, but Jonathan kicked the ball to him anyway.

31
00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:16.724
A Silver Bomber got it and made a long, high pass to a teammate.

32
00:03:16.725 --> 00:03:25.037
That guy headed the ball to another teammate, who passed it to another teammate.

33
00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:28.540
The Silver Bombers kept passing the ball up the field.

34
00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:35.459
"They work so well together. No ball hogs on their team!" Jonathan thought as he ran to defend the ball.

35
00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:44.262
But it was useless. Thanks to their excellent passing, the Silver Bombers scored a goal.

36
00:03:44.263 --> 00:03:47.380
"Nooo!" Coach Wattenbarger yelled.

37
00:03:47.381 --> 00:03:50.699
Jonathan kicked the grass in frustration.

38
00:03:50.699 --> 00:03:55.929
Max stood next to him at the kickoff. "Sorry I missed your pass, Jonathan."

39
00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:00.508
"You were double-teamed, but your dad still made me pass to you," Jonathan grumbled.

40
00:04:00.509 --> 00:04:02.992
Max didn't respond.

41
00:04:02.992 --> 00:04:13.406
The game continued with three substitute Silver Bombers and no substitute Wattenbargers. Team Wattenbarger kept passing Max the ball.

42
00:04:13.407 --> 00:04:19.072
But with the Silver Bombers double-teaming him, he kept losing the ball, and his father kept yelling at him.

43
00:04:19.073 --> 00:04:30.390
Jonathan was grateful to hear the referee's whistle announce halftime. The team, dripping with sweat, staggered off the field.

44
00:04:30.391 --> 00:04:35.888
"I'm miserable. I should quit the team like the twins did," Jonathan moaned.

45
00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:40.720
Carlos shook his head. "You can't quit. We need you."

46
00:04:40.721 --> 00:04:47.633
"You don't need me to watch Max hog the ball. I know he's the best player in the league." Jonathan rolled his eyes.

47
00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:51.459
"But even Max can't score when he's double-teamed."

48
00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:57.450
Carlos shot a look at the coach and then lowered his voice. "You and I know how to play soccer together.

49
00:04:57.451 --> 00:05:02.616
The next time Max is double-teamed, I'll pass you the ball, and you can take a shot at the goal."

50
00:05:02.617 --> 00:05:05.383
"Coach would get mad," Jonathan said.

51
00:05:05.384 --> 00:05:09.205
Carlos shrugged. "He won't be mad if you score a goal."

52
00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:17.442
"He might still be mad," Jonathan said. "But you know what—that's a great idea, Carlos. Let's try it in the second half!"

53
00:05:17.443 --> 00:05:25.419
At the halftime meeting, Coach Wattenbarger folded his arms across his chest. "Max, you played horribly today."

54
00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.252
"I was double-teamed most of the time," Max muttered.

55
00:05:29.253 --> 00:05:34.267
"Stop making excuses! You'll never get a college scholarship that way."

56
00:05:34.268 --> 00:05:40.337
Jonathan pitied Max even more than he pitied himself. Max's father was so hard on Max.

57
00:05:40.338 --> 00:05:46.090
During the second half, Team Wattenbarger panted and sweated while the Silver Bombers substituted players.

58
00:05:46.091 --> 00:05:50.159
Max tried hard to score, but he was constantly double-teamed.

59
00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.743
Once Carlos got the ball, he kicked it to Jonathan.

60
00:05:55.744 --> 00:05:59.668
"Cho! Pass to Max!" the coach yelled.

61
00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:11.476
Jonathan glanced at Max, who had two Silver Bombers drawn to him like magnets. Instead of passing, Jonathan took a long shot toward the goal.

62
00:06:11.477 --> 00:06:14.758
"Go, Johnnyboy!" his mother yelled from the sideline.

63
00:06:14.759 --> 00:06:17.229
Jonathan cringed.

64
00:06:17.229 --> 00:06:24.036
The Silver Bomber goalie caught the ball and kicked it hard down the field.

65
00:06:24.037 --> 00:06:28.621
His teammate headed it to another teammate, who headed it to one of their forwards.

66
00:06:28.622 --> 00:06:37.114
The forward trapped it, dribbled it, and then kicked it right into the Wattenbargers' goal.

67
00:06:37.115 --> 00:06:40.781
"Bad play, Carlos and Jonathan!" the coach bellowed.

68
00:06:40.782 --> 00:06:45.010
Jonathan's stomach sank. It sure was a bad play.

69
00:06:45.011 --> 00:06:53.598
Jonathan felt nothing but relief when the game ended a few minutes later. The Wattenbargers had lost, 0–2.

70
00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:59.490
As he walked off the field, Jonathan apologized to Carlos.

71
00:06:59.491 --> 00:07:01.530
"Sorry I missed that shot."

72
00:07:01.531 --> 00:07:05.199
"It was my idea," Carlos said.

73
00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:12.832
The coach called the team over to him. He leaned forward, giving Jonathan a close-up view of his angry red face and big bald head.

74
00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:20.101
"You boys were terrible today! And, Max, you need more practice. No video games for you this week."

75
00:07:20.102 --> 00:07:21.766
Max hung his head.

76
00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:26.577
After the team meeting, Jonathan went over to Max.

77
00:07:26.577 --> 00:07:32.482
"Your dad needs to give you a break. It wasn't your fault that you were double-teamed and we had no substitutes."

78
00:07:32.483 --> 00:07:39.585
Max looked surprised—and grateful. "Thanks, Jonathan," he said. "I'm glad you're on my team."

79
00:07:39.586 --> 00:07:51.356
"Me too," Jonathan said, surprised to realize that he meant it. He just wished they had a different coach.
